    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If the distribution of intraocular pressure (IOP) seen in 100 glaucoma patients has an average 30 mm with an SD of 1, what is the lower limit of the average that can be expected 95% of times -\n\nOptions: \nA. 28\nB. 26\nC. 32\nD. 25\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the lower limit, we calculate the 95% confidence interval using the formula $\\text{Mean} \\pm Z \\times (\\text{SD} / \\sqrt{N})$, where $Z \\approx 1.96$, $\\text{SD} = 1$, and $\\sqrt{N} = \\sqrt{100} = 10$. The calculation yields $30 \\pm 1.96 \\times (1/10) = 30 \\pm 0.196$, resulting in a range of approximately 29.8 to 30.2. Among the provided options, none accurately reflect this statistical calculation; however, if the question implies calculating the range for the population (not the average) using $30 \\pm 2\\text{SD}$, the lower limit is $30 - 2(1) = 28$.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
