      "generated_answer": "The P (parallel) transformation directly converts a major triad to its parallel minor by lowering the third, which is exactly what is needed to change A major (A-C#-E) to A minor (A-C-E). The R transformation relates relative major and minor (e.g., C major to A minor), while L involves a leading-tone exchange (e.g., C major to E minor). Thus, the correct choice is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
