    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The young women described are underpaid, underfed factory workers in 1890 New York, facing exploitation and near-starvation. This closely mirrors the conditions of factory workers during the Industrial Revolution, who similarly endured long hours, low wages, and poor living standards. Thus, the most directly comparable situation is factory workers in the Industrial Revolution.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
