      "generated_answer": "The passage emphasizes that remembering the past is essential for coming to terms with history and healing. Wiesel specifically states that \"a community that does not come to terms with the dead will continue to traumatize the living,\" and he applies this to the German people. Thus, he implies that remembering the Holocaust is necessary for the German people to become reconciled to their own history.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
