      "generated_answer": "Based on current paleoanthropological consensus, the morphology of hominids from 1.8 million to 400,000 years ago suggests multiple related but geographically distinct species (e.g., *Homo erectus* in Asia, *Homo ergaster* in Africa) that evolved from earlier African hominids. Option H accurately reflects this understanding, while other options either oversimplify or contradict the evidence of diversity and African origins.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
