      "generated_answer": "Dorothea Dix's advocacy for the humane treatment of the mentally ill was part of the broader social reform movements fueled by the Second Great Awakening, which emphasized moral perfectionism and humanitarianism. Her efforts directly stemmed from the religious and reformist zeal of that era, aiming to address societal injustices. Therefore, the correct answer is E.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
