      "generated_answer": "The United States Senate rejected the Treaty of Versailles primarily due to concerns that the League of Nations would entangle the U.S. in European conflicts and undermine its sovereignty. This aligns with option C, as the treaty required increased American involvement in European affairs, which many senators opposed. The other options are historically inaccurate regarding the Senate's final action.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
