    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Brown v. Board of Education decision addressed the failure of Reconstruction to guarantee equal protection under the law, as segregation persisted despite the Fourteenth Amendment. This ruling sought to fulfill the unfulfilled promises of Reconstruction by ending de jure segregation in public schools. Thus, the correct answer is Reconstruction.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
