      "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{H}.\n\nDuring the Qing Dynasty, particularly under the Canton System in effect during this period, European merchants were restricted to operating in specific port cities, most notably Canton (Guangzhou). While the provided text highlights the emperor's attitude of superiority and the tribute system, the historical practice of regulating foreign trade throughout the 18th and 19th centuries was characterized by these geographic restrictions.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 361,
        "output_tokens": 90,
        "total_tokens": 451
      },
