- 1)(\\alpha + 1) = 8 f(1)f(-1).\n$$  \nSince $f(1) = 1 + 1 + 1 = 3$, $f(-1) = -1 -1 + 1 = -1$, so product is $8 \\cdot 3 \\cdot (-1) = -24$.  \nHence $\\prod_{j=0}^6 f(\\omega^j) = -24$, and $\\prod_{k=0}^6 (\\omega^{3k} + \\omega^k + 1) = -24$.  \n\nWait—check: For $k=0$, term is $3$, and product over all $k=0$ to $6$ is indeed $\\prod f(\\omega^k) = -24$. So answer is $\\boxed{-24}$.",
