    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The permuterm index works by storing every rotation of each term (with a special end-of-term symbol) so that a wildcard query can be rewritten with the * at the end and looked up via dictionary search. Because a term of length \\(n\\) produces \\(n\\) distinct rotations that must all be kept, the dictionary grows by a factor roughly proportional to the average term length; this size explosion is the most commonly cited drawback in standard IR references. The other options do not correspond to documented disadvantages of the technique: implementation is straightforward rotations plus ordinary dictionary lookup (eliminating A), collisions are not an inherent issue (eliminating B), and spelling correction is simply outside the method’s intended purpose (eliminating D).\n\n\\boxed{C}",
