      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef countSubMultisets(nums, l, r):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    \n    # Count frequency of each number\n    from collections import Counter\n    count = Counter(nums)\n    \n    # dp[i] will store the number of ways to achieve sum i\n    # We only need to track sums up to r (at most 20000)\n    dp = [0] * (r + 1)\n    dp[0] = 1  # One way to make sum 0 (empty set)\n    \n    # Process each unique number\n    for num, freq in count.items():\n        if num > r:\n            continue\n            \n        # We need to update dp array from right to left to avoid using updated values\n        # Create a new state for this number\n        new_dp = dp[:]\n        \n        # For each possible sum\n        for current_sum in range(r + 1):\n            if dp[current_sum] == 0:\n                continue\n                \n            # Try adding 1, 2, ..., freq occurrences of num\n            for occurrences in range(1, freq + 1):\n                new_sum = current_sum + num * occurrences\n                if new_sum > r:\n                    break\n                new_dp[new_sum] = (new_dp[new_sum] + dp[current_sum]) % MOD\n        \n        dp = new_dp\n    \n    # Sum all ways to achieve sums in range [l, r]\n    result = 0\n    for i in range(l, r + 1):\n        result = (result + dp[i]) % MOD\n    \n    return result\n```",
