      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport collections\n\ndef minimumGroups(nums):\n    if not nums:\n        return 0\n    freq = collections.Counter(nums)\n    freqs = list(freq.values())\n    n = len(nums)\n    d = len(freqs)\n    if d == 0:\n        return 0\n    max_f = max(freqs)\n    MAX = max_f\n    # Build sum_max[s] = sum floor(f / s) for s=1 to MAX\n    diff_max = [0] * (MAX + 2)\n    for f in freqs:\n        i = 1\n        while i <= min(f, MAX):\n            q = f // i\n            r = min(f // q, MAX)\n            diff_max[i] += q\n            if r + 1 <= MAX + 1:\n                diff_max[r + 1] -= q\n            i = r + 1\n    sum_max = [0] * (MAX + 2)\n    cur = 0\n    for s in range(1, MAX + 1):\n        cur += diff_max[s]\n        sum_max[s] = cur\n    # Build sum_ceil[t] = sum ceil(f / t) for t=1 to MAX+1\n    diff_ceil = [0] * (MAX + 3)\n    for f in freqs:\n        fp = f - 1\n        if fp > 0:\n            i = 1\n            while i <= min(fp, MAX + 1):\n                q = fp // i\n                r = min(fp // q, MAX + 1)\n                diff_ceil[i] += q\n                if r + 1 <= MAX + 2:\n                    diff_ceil[r + 1] -= q\n                i = r + 1\n    sum_ceil = [0] * (MAX + 3)\n    cur = 0\n    for t in range(1, MAX + 2):\n        cur += diff_ceil[t]\n        sum_ceil[t] = cur + d\n    # Find minimal g\n    ans = n\n    for s in range(1, MAX + 1):\n        left = n // (s + 1) + 1\n        right = n // s\n        if left > right:\n            continue\n        minm = sum_ceil[s + 1]\n        maxm = sum_max[s]\n        if minm > maxm:\n            continue\n        lg = max(left, minm)\n        hg = min(right, maxm)\n        if lg <= hg:\n            ans = min(ans, lg)\n    return ans\n```",
