      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findMinimumOperations(s1: str, s2: str, s3: str) -> int:\n    # To make strings equal by deleting from the right, they must share a common prefix.\n    # If the first characters are not the same, they can never be made equal.\n    if s1[0] != s2[0] or s1[0] != s3[0] or s2[0] != s3[0]:\n        return -1\n    \n    # Find the length of the longest common prefix among the three strings\n    min_len = min(len(s1), len(s2), len(s3))\n    common_prefix_len = 0\n    \n    for i in range(min_len):\n        if s1[i] == s2[i] == s3[i]:\n            common_prefix_len += 1\n        else:\n            break\n            \n    # The total operations needed is the sum of characters to delete from each string\n    # to reduce them all to the length of the longest common prefix.\n    total_len = len(s1) + len(s2) + len(s3)\n    return total_len - (3 * common_prefix_len)\n```",
