      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef minimum_coins(prices: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the minimum number of coins needed to acquire all fruits.\n    \n    The fruit market offer: purchasing the i-th fruit (1-indexed) at prices[i-1]\n    allows you to take the next i fruits for free. You can still choose to purchase\n    a fruit even if it is available for free, to trigger its offer.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(prices)\n    # Make the array 1-indexed for easier reasoning\n    prices_1based = [0] + prices\n    # dp[i] = minimum cost to acquire first i fruits\n    dp = [float('inf')] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0\n    \n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # The last purchased fruit j must cover fruit i: 2*j >= i  =>  j >= ceil(i/2)\n        start = (i + 1) // 2\n        for j in range(start, i + 1):\n            dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[j - 1] + prices_1based[j])\n            \n    return dp[n]\n```",
