    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumCoins(prices: list[int]) -> int:\n    n = len(prices)\n    # dp[i] represents the minimum coins to acquire all fruits from index i to n.\n    # We use a 1-indexed approach for i to match the problem description.\n    # dp[n+1] is the base case (0 coins needed when no fruits are left).\n    dp = [0] * (n + 2)\n    \n    for i in range(n, 0, -1):\n        # If we purchase the i-th fruit (prices[i-1]), \n        # we can get the next i fruits for free.\n        # This means we cover fruits from i up to i + i.\n        # The next fruit we *must* consider purchasing starts at index j,\n        # where i + 1 <= j <= 2*i + 1.\n        \n        # If 2*i >= n, we can cover all remaining fruits by purchasing fruit i.\n        if 2 * i >= n:\n            dp[i] = prices[i - 1]\n        else:\n            # Otherwise, we find the minimum cost among all possible next \n            # purchases within the range we could have skipped.\n            res = float('inf')\n            for j in range(i + 1, 2 * i + 2):\n                res = min(res, dp[j])\n            dp[i] = prices[i - 1] + res\n            \n    return dp[1]\n```",
