uming we start at position i and no prior offers cover position i.\n\nFor each position i, we must buy fruit i (since it's not covered), which costs `prices[i-1]` and covers positions i+1 to 2*i.\n\nThen we need to consider where the next uncovered fruit is.\n\n```python\ndef minimumCoins(prices):\n    n = len(prices)\n    # dp[i] represents minimum cost to acquire fruits from position i to n (1-indexed)\n    # We'll use 1-indexed thinking but 0-indexed array\n    memo = {}\n    \n    def dp(pos):\n        if pos > n:\n            return 0\n        if pos in memo:\n            return memo[pos]\n        \n        # We must purchase the fruit at position pos (since we're at this position)\n        # Buying fruit at pos gives us next pos fruits for free\n        # So fruits pos+1, pos+2, ..., pos+pos are free\n        max_covered = pos + pos\n        \n        # The next position we need to pay for is max_covered + 1\n        # But we can also choose to buy fruits before that to extend coverage\n        # Actually, we need to try buying at each position from pos+1 to max_covered+1\n        # if we want to optimize further\n        \n        # Simple approach: buy current fruit, then solve for the next uncovered position\n        min_cost = prices[pos - 1] + dp(max_covered + 1)\n        \n        # But we might want to buy some of the \"free\" fruits to get better offers\n        # Let's try buying at each position in the free range\n        for buy_pos in range(pos + 1, max_covered + 2):\n            if buy_pos > n:\n                break\n            # Buy fruit at buy_pos, which costs prices[buy_pos-1]\n            # This gives us coverage for next buy_pos fruits\n            coverage_from_buy = buy_pos + buy_pos\n            cost = prices[pos - 1] + prices[buy_pos - 1] + dp(coverage_from_buy + 1)\n            min_cost = min(min_cost, cost)\n        \n        # Actually, we need to consider that after buying pos, \n        # we can strategically buy any subset of the