      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findMissingAndRepeatedValues(grid):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the repeating and missing numbers in an n x n grid.\n    \n    Args:\n    grid (List[List[int]]): n x n matrix containing numbers from 1 to n^2.\n    \n    Returns:\n    List[int]: A list [a, b] where a is the repeated number and b is the missing number.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(grid)\n    total_elements = n * n\n    \n    # Use a frequency map (or set) to track occurrences\n    # Since constraints are small (n <= 50), a frequency array is efficient\n    counts = [0] * (total_elements + 1)\n    \n    for row in grid:\n        for val in row:\n            counts[val] += 1\n            \n    a = -1\n    b = -1\n    \n    for i in range(1, total_elements + 1):\n        if counts[i] == 2:\n            a = i\n        elif counts[i] == 0:\n            b = i\n            \n        # Break early if both found\n        if a != -1 and b != -1:\n            break\n            \n    return [a, b]\n```",
