      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef largestPerimeter(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    To find the largest possible perimeter of a polygon:\n    1. Sort the numbers in ascending order.\n    2. Maintain a running sum of all elements seen so far.\n    3. Iterate through the sorted array. For each element nums[i], if the sum of \n       all previous elements (0 to i-1) is greater than nums[i], then a \n       polygon can be formed using all elements up to i.\n    4. Since we want the largest perimeter, we update our answer as we go.\n    \"\"\"\n    nums.sort()\n    total_sum = 0\n    max_perimeter = -1\n    \n    for i in range(len(nums)):\n        # If we have at least 2 sides already (to make a polygon of at least 3 sides)\n        # and the sum of those sides is greater than the current side (the potential longest side)\n        if i >= 2 and total_sum > nums[i]:\n            max_perimeter = total_sum + nums[i]\n        \n        total_sum += nums[i]\n        \n    return max_perimeter\n```",
