    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef canTraverseAllPairs(nums: list[int]) -> bool:\n    n = len(nums)\n    if n == 1:\n        return True\n    \n    # If any number is 1 and there are multiple numbers, traversal is impossible\n    # because gcd(1, x) = 1, which is not > 1.\n    for x in nums:\n        if x == 1:\n            return False\n            \n    # Use Disjoint Set Union (DSU) to group indices connected by common factors\n    parent = list(range(n))\n    \n    def find(i):\n        if parent[i] == i:\n            return i\n        parent[i] = find(parent[i])\n        return parent[i]\n    \n    def union(i, j):\n        root_i = find(i)\n        root_j = find(j)\n        if root_i != root_j:\n            parent[root_i] = root_j\n            return True\n        return False\n\n    # prime_to_index maps a prime factor to the index of the first number \n    # encountered that is divisible by that prime.\n    prime_to_index = {}\n    max_val = max(nums)\n    \n    # Precompute smallest prime factor (SPF) for efficient factorization\n    spf = list(range(max_val + 1))\n    for i in range(2, int(max_val**0.5) + 1):\n        if spf[i] == i:\n            for j in range(i*i, max_val + 1, i):\n                if spf[j] == j:\n                    spf[j] = i\n\n    for i, val in enumerate(nums):\n        temp = val\n        while temp > 1:\n            p = spf[temp]\n            if p in prime_to_index:\n                union(i, prime_to_index[p])\n            else:\n                prime_to_index[p] = i\n            # Divide out all instances of the prime p\n            while temp % p == 0:\n                temp //= p\n                \n    # Check if all indices belong to the same connected component\n    root = find(0)\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if find(i) != root:\n            return False\n            \n    return True\n```",
