least `max(0, count1 + count2 - M)` logo T-shirts for this segment\n\nBut since the same logo T-shirts can be used across different segments (they get washed on '0' days), the total number of logo T-shirts needed is the maximum needed in any single segment.\n\nWait, that's not quite right either. Let me think more carefully.\n\nActually, the logo T-shirts can be reused across segments because washing on '0' days makes all worn T-shirts available again. So the constraint is indeed per segment, and we need enough logo T-shirts to handle the worst-case segment.\n\nBut there's also the constraint that event days (2) must use logo T-shirts. So in any segment, we need at least `count2` logo T-shirts.\n\nLet me formalize:\n\nFor a segment with `count1` meal days and `count2` event days:\n- We need at least `count2` logo T-shirts (for the event days)\n- Total T-shirts needed = `count1 + count2`\n- We have M plain T-shirts, so we need at least `max(count2, count1 + count2 - M)` logo T-shirts\n\nSince logo T-shirts can be reused across segments (due to washing on '0' days), the answer is the maximum of this value across all segments.\n\nLet me verify with the samples:\n\n**Sample 1:** S = \"112022\", M = 1\n- Segment 1: \"112\" → count1=2, count2=1 → need max(1, 2+1-1)=max(1,2)=2\n- Segment 2: \"22\" → count1=0, count2=2 → need max(2, 0+2-1)=max(2,1)=2\n- Maximum = 2 ✓\n\n**Sample 2:** S = \"222\", M = 1\n- Segment: \"222\" → count1=0, count2=3 → need max(3, 0+3-1)=max(3,2)=3 ✓\n\n**Sample 3:** S = \"01\", M = 1\n- Segment 1: \"\" (before first '0') → count1=0, count2=0 → need 0\n- Segment 2: \"1\" → count1=1, count2=0 → need max(0, 1+0-1)=max(0,0)=0\n- Maximum = 0 ✓\n\nLet me code this approach.\n\n```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split('\\n')\n    if not data or not data[0].strip():\n        return\n    n, m = map(int, data[0].split())\n    s = data[1].strip() if len(data) > 1 else \"\"\n    \n    # Split the string into segments separated by '0'\n    segments = s.split('0')\n    \n    max_logo_needed = 0\n    \n    for segment in segments:\n        count1 = segment.count('1')\n        count2 = segment.count('2')\n        \n        # We need at least count2 logo T-shirts for the event days\n        # Total T-shirts needed for the segment is count1 + count2\n        # We have m plain T-shirts, so we need at least (count1 + count2 - m) logo T-shirts if this is positive\n        logo_needed = max(count2, count1 + count2 - m)\n        max_logo_needed = max(max_logo_needed, logo_needed)\n    \n    print(max_logo_needed)\n\nsolve()\n```",
