      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef solve():\n    input = sys.stdin.readline\n    H, W = map(int, input().split())\n    grid = [list(input().strip()) for _ in range(H)]\n\n    # component ids for green cells, -1 for red or unassigned\n    comp = [[-1] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    dirs = [(1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, 1), (0, -1)]\n    comp_id = 0\n\n    # BFS to assign component ids to green cells\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '#' and comp[i][j] == -1:\n                queue = deque([(i, j)])\n                comp[i][j] = comp_id\n                while queue:\n                    x, y = queue.popleft()\n                    for dx, dy in dirs:\n                        ni, nj = x + dx, y + dy\n                        if 0 <= ni < H and 0 <= nj < W and grid[ni][nj] == '#' and comp[ni][nj] == -1:\n                            comp[ni][nj] = comp_id\n                            queue.append((ni, nj))\n                comp_id += 1\n\n    comp0 = comp_id           # initial number of green components\n    R = 0                     # number of red cells\n    sum_k = 0                 # sum of k_r over all red cells\n\n    # Process each red cell\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '.':\n                R += 1\n                neigh_ids = set()\n                for dx, dy in dirs:\n                    ni, nj = i + dx, j + dy\n                    if 0 <= ni < H and 0 <= nj < W and grid[ni][nj] == '#':\n                        neigh_ids.add(comp[ni][nj])\n                sum_k += len(neigh_ids)\n\n    MOD = 998244353\n    invR = pow(R, MOD - 2, MOD)\n    ans = (comp0 + 1 - sum_k * invR) % MOD\n    print(ans)\n```",
