      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    H = int(data[0])\n    W = int(data[1])\n    grid = data[2:]\n    MOD = 998244353\n    \n    # Count red cells\n    R = sum(row.count('.') for row in grid)\n    \n    # Union-Find structure for green cells\n    parent = [-1] * (H * W)\n    \n    def find(x):\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\n            x = parent[x]\n        return x\n    \n    def union(a, b):\n        ra, rb = find(a), find(b)\n        if ra != rb:\n            parent[rb] = ra\n    \n    # Initialize green cells\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '#':\n                idx = i * W + j\n                parent[idx] = idx\n                \n    # Union adjacent green cells (right and down)\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '#':\n                idx = i * W + j\n                if j + 1 < W and grid[i][j + 1] == '#':\n                    union(idx, idx + 1)\n                if i + 1 < H and grid[i + 1][j] == '#':\n                    union(idx, idx + W)\n    \n    # Count distinct green components\n    roots = set()\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '#':\n                roots.add(find(i * W + j))\n    C = len(roots)\n    \n    # For each red cell, count distinct adjacent green components\n    sum_c = 0\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '.':\n                adj = set()\n                if i > 0 and grid[i - 1][j] == '#':\n                    adj.add(find((i - 1) * W + j))\n                if i + 1 < H and grid[i + 1][j] == '#':\n                    adj.add(find((i + 1) * W + j))\n                if j > 0 and grid[i][j - 1] == '#':\n                    adj.add(find(i * W + (j - 1)))\n                if j + 1 < W and grid[i][j + 1] == '#':\n                    adj.add(find(i * W + (j + 1)))\n                sum_c += len(adj)\n    \n    # Expected value = ((C + 1) * R - sum_c) / R  (mod MOD)\n    num = ((C + 1) * R - sum_c) % MOD\n    inv_R = pow(R, MOD - 2, MOD)\n    ans = (num * inv_R) % MOD\n    print(ans)\n\n```",
